From: DBY-W09 contributors <contributors@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: reboot-mode: only write modes on restart

The reboot notifier chain is also called for halt and power-off, with a
NULL command. The reboot-mode notifier interprets that command as the
normal mode and writes its magic even though no restart was requested.

Writing a reboot reason on shutdown is unnecessary. On boards mapping
normal mode to recovery, it also causes the next power-on after shutdown
to enter recovery instead of the normal boot path.

Only handle SYS_RESTART so that halt and power-off leave the reboot mode
untouched. Keep command lookup and explicit restart modes unchanged.

Signed-off-by: DBY-W09 contributors <contributors@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
@@ -107,6 +107,9 @@ static int reboot_mode_notify(struct notifier_block *this,
 	struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot;
 	unsigned int magic;

+	if (mode != SYS_RESTART)
+		return NOTIFY_DONE;
+
 	reboot = container_of(this, struct reboot_mode_driver, reboot_notifier);
 	magic = get_reboot_mode_magic(reboot, cmd);
 	if (magic)
